# Tengine — CoreX (ivcore11) FULL TEST-SUITE re-run (completeness correction, v3)
# Device: GPU 1 (Iluvatar BI-V150), CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1
#
# v3: onnx 1.22.0 is now genuinely installed, so the ONNX node conformance data
# needed by the 75 test_onnx_op_* ctests was GENERATED for real and the tests were
# actually executed (they reach inference). See parts below.
#
#   PART A1 — data generation: for each op, take the ONNX backend node model
#             (onnx/backend/test/data/node/<node>/) and convert model.onnx -> Tengine
#             onnx.tmfile with Tengine's own convert_tool; copy test_data_set_*/*.pb.
#             10 ops whose stock models use opset-25 (axes/pads as inputs) or omit a
#             required attr were regenerated at a Tengine-parseable opset (see
#             corex_port/test/regen_hard_ops.py).
#   PART A2 — full ctest collection actually executed (75 ONNX op tests, Tengine CPU
#             REFERENCE backend). 68 pass, 7 fail.
#   PART B  — CUDA-backend on-GPU parity (9 models) — the CUDA-exercising portion, 9/9.
#
# The 7 failures are pre-existing Tengine CPU-reference-backend defects (NOT CoreX/CUDA,
# NOT data): 4 conv output all-zeros (harness fills weight buffer AFTER prerun_graph, so
# Tengine prepacks zero weights); 3 (batchnorm_example/dropout_default/pad_reflect) reach
# inference then abort with heap corruption at teardown (dropout even prints 'test pass').
################################################################################

